      "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nAdds a \u201csoft confirmation\u201d interaction for skipping tasks in the UI dashboard\u2019s `TaskSequencer`, intended to reduce accidental skips, and updates accessibility tests/docs to reflect the UX change.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Introduces a 3-second, second-click confirmation flow for the \u201cSkip\u201d action (icon swap + pulse animation + button variant change).\n- Updates the `PredictionPanel` accessibility test query to match the current accessible labeling.\n- Documents the \u201cSoft Confirmation\u201d pattern in the Palette journal.\n\n**Files changed:**  \n- `ui-dashboard/src/components/TaskSequencer.tsx`  \n- `ui-dashboard/src/components/__tests__/Accessibility.test.tsx`  \n- `.Jules/palette.md`\n\n**How to test:**\n- `cd ui-dashboard && npm test`\n- (Optional) `cd ui-dashboard && npm run lint`\n\n**Risk notes:**\n- The skip-confirmation state needs to be canceled when the current task changes; otherwise the \u201csecond click required\u201d safety can be bypassed in some flows.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 3 out of 3 changed files in this pull request and generated 3 comments.\n\n| File | Description |\n| ---- | ----------- |\n| ui-dashboard/src/components/TaskSequencer.tsx | Adds skip \u201csoft confirmation\u201d state, animation keyframes, and updated Skip button styling/labels. |\n| ui-dashboard/src/components/__tests__/Accessibility.test.tsx | Adjusts a11y test expectations for `PredictionPanel` and the `TaskSequencer` skip label logic. |\n| .Jules/palette.md | Records the soft-confirmation UX pattern in the Palette journal. |\n\n\n\n\n",
